  "worked_solution": "We need to isolate $x,$ so we will treat the other variables $w$ and $y$ as constants. We can use the addition and multiplication principles to solve for $x.$\n\nFirst, we subtract $5w$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5w+7x \\\\ y-5w & =5w+7x-5w \\\\ y-5w & =7x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x & =y-5w \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & =\\frac{y-5w}{7} \\\\ x & =\\frac{y-5w}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
